## Interface: 16001
## Title: ItemTree
## Notes: What is this item used for? Crafting chains, quests, disenchanting, drops and vendors, with New and Changed flags compared with Classic Era.
## Author: Rockjaw Bonesnapper Co
## Version: v0.1.19
## SavedVariables: ItemTreeDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: ItemTreeCharDB
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ItemTree\Art\minimap
## AddonCompartmentFunc: ItemTree_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## X-Website: https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/itemtree
## X-License: All Rights Reserved
## X-Category: Professions
# Load order only, and every one of them is optional: Providers\ reads a source database the
# player has already installed and ships none of it. The names are addon FOLDERS, which is what
# the client matches: AllTheThings\AllTheThings.toc and Questie\Questie.toc.
## OptionalDeps: AllTheThings, Questie
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1711215
## X-Wago-ID: 5NRgev63
## X-WoWI-ID:

# Interface 16001 is the WoW Forever beta (client 1.60.1, product wow_classic_beta). ItemTree
# is listed for the Forever client only at this stage, which is what keeps the addon sites from
# offering it to Classic Era players. Adding another flavour later is one more number on the
# Interface line above plus the notes in docs/release.md. Classic Era 1.15.9 stays the data
# baseline the New and Changed flags compare against, which is a fact about the data, not a
# client the addon is listed for.

Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua

Locales\enUS.lua

Core\Init.lua
# Brief G1: the error boundary, before anything that runs under it.
Core\Guard.lua
# Brief OPT4: the small helpers several files share (numbers, trim, saved variable sizes, client
# lookups), before every file that takes them. After Guard.lua, which must stay second.
Core\Util.lua
# Brief BQ13: the demo state (what the addon thinks the character is, memory only). Read at call time
# by Keep, Gear, the API and the tooltip, so it only has to load before the commands run.
Core\Demo.lua
Core\Data.lua
# The on demand loader for the optional addon folders (brief PR3), before the stubs that use it.
Core\Modules.lua
Core\Edges.lua
Core\Confidence.lua
Core\Privacy.lua
Core\Graph.lua
Core\Prices.lua
# Brief K20c: the price formula, read by Core\Keep.lua for the Bar.
Core\PriceFormula.lua
# Brief K25: the consumable facts over the ItemEffects data; Core\Keep.lua reads them where they ship.
Core\Consumables.lua
Core\Keep.lua
# Brief K20-facts: the gear and disenchant value facts; Core\Keep.lua reads both (brief K20-wire).
Core\Gear.lua
Core\DisenchantValue.lua
Core\Diff.lua
Core\ViewModel.lua
Core\Skills.lua
# Brief TP1 (QA item 210): the professions a character tracks without having them, read at call time by
